function help80(){
 const panel=Q('#helpPanel');if(!panel)return;const V='v8.3.70',topics=[{"id":"overview","cat":"Getting started","title":"What the logger records","summary":"Understand the data model before using capture, imports or Bank Compare.","body":"<p>Albion Loot Logger records loot events into sessions. A record can contain the looter, guild, alliance, item ID and name, enchantment, quality, category, quantity, source, timestamp, zone, price snapshot, deposit state and edit history. Views may group records, but the underlying event history remains available for validation, timeline and exports.</p><p>Unknown-source events are skipped rather than silently assigned to the wrong player. Duplicate protection prevents the same network event or imported row from being counted twice.</p>"},{"id":"requirements","cat":"Getting started","title":"Npcap and first-time requirements","summary":"Install packet capture support and understand the automatic compatibility warning.","body":"<ol><li>Install a supported Npcap version with WinPcap-compatible packet capture enabled.</li><li>Run the logger, then start Albion Online and enter the game world.</li><li>When Npcap is missing, incompatible, outdated or a newer required version is detected, the logger offers the official Npcap download page.</li><li>Use <b>Advanced → Capture health</b> to verify raw packets and Albion UDP traffic.</li></ol>"},{"id":"first-run","cat":"Getting started","title":"First successful capture","summary":"Confirm the complete path from network packet to visible loot.","body":"<ol><li>Wait until Capture is active and Albion is detected.</li><li>Loot one known item from another player or an allowed source.</li><li>Confirm Raw packets and Albion UDP increase.</li><li>Confirm Last loot resets to zero and the player/item appears on Loot.</li><li>Open item details to verify source and time, then save or export the session.</li></ol>"},{"id":"navigation","cat":"Getting started","title":"Pages and navigation","summary":"Know what each left-side page is for.","body":"<table><thead><tr><th>Control</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Loot</td><td>Live session, player cards, search, groups, file loading and exports.</td></tr><tr><td>Bank compare</td><td>Compare expected loot with one or more bank exports.</td></tr><tr><td>Bank logs compare</td><td>Compare temporary chest responsibility with a final bank log.</td></tr><tr><td>Options</td><td>Themes, background images, capture filters, roster and page visibility.</td></tr><tr><td>Analytics</td><td>Session totals, top players/items, prices and recent activity.</td></tr><tr><td>Advanced</td><td>Capture health, simulation, skipped events, unknown items and session tools.</td></tr><tr><td>Workflow</td><td>Validation, corrections, timeline, archives, prices, backups and diagnostics.</td></tr><tr><td>Help</td><td>This searchable code-backed manual.</td></tr></tbody></table>"},{"id":"status","cat":"Getting started","title":"Top status and bottom status bar","summary":"Read the application state without opening diagnostics.","body":"<p>The top notification reports capture problems such as a stream with no packet callbacks. The bottom status bar summarizes capture, Albion, session ID, event count, unknown/skipped count and last loot. These indicators update independently of the currently selected page.</p>"},{"id":"capture-health","cat":"Live capture","title":"Capture Health explained","summary":"Interpret every health indicator and diagnose the failing stage.","body":"<table><thead><tr><th>Control</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Capture</td><td>Packet listener state: starting, active, waiting or failed.</td></tr><tr><td>Albion</td><td>Whether an Albion process is detected.</td></tr><tr><td>Raw packets</td><td>All traffic received by the selected capture interface.</td></tr><tr><td>Albion UDP</td><td>Packets recognized as Albion traffic.</td></tr><tr><td>Photon/events</td><td>Decoded protocol messages and loot responses.</td></tr><tr><td>Last loot</td><td>Age of the newest loot event in days, hours, minutes and seconds.</td></tr><tr><td>Catalog</td><td>Known item definitions used for names, categories and icons.</td></tr><tr><td>Lookup service</td><td>Availability of optional player/guild lookups.</td></tr></tbody></table>"},{"id":"sessions","cat":"Live capture","title":"Sessions and lifecycle","summary":"Start, end, clear and automate event sessions safely.","body":"<p>A session isolates one event and stores its start/end time, players, guilds, loot, metadata, notes and value snapshot. <b>New session</b> starts clean data. <b>Clear session</b> removes current visible session data after confirmation. Session Manager can archive before switching.</p><ul><li>Optional startup automation creates a new session when the logger starts.</li><li>Optional Albion lifecycle automation can end a session when Albion closes and start another when Albion opens.</li><li>Inactivity automation can finish a session after the configured quiet period.</li><li>Pause view freezes visual updates only; capture continues.</li></ul>"},{"id":"loot-controls","cat":"Loot page","title":"Loot toolbar","summary":"Use every action in the live-session command bar.","body":"<table><thead><tr><th>Control</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>New session</td><td>Starts a clean event session.</td></tr><tr><td>Pause view</td><td>Stops visual rerendering without stopping capture.</td></tr><tr><td>Expand/Collapse</td><td>Opens or closes all player cards.</td></tr><tr><td>Copy selected</td><td>Copies checked items when selection is available.</td></tr><tr><td>Copy summary</td><td>Copies a readable player/item summary.</td></tr><tr><td>Export TXT</td><td>Opens a save location and writes the full loot report.</td></tr><tr><td>Refresh items</td><td>Refreshes item definitions, icons and visible rendering.</td></tr><tr><td>Clear session</td><td>Clears the current event after confirmation.</td></tr><tr><td>Exit</td><td>Closes the application cleanly.</td></tr></tbody></table>"},{"id":"player-cards","cat":"Loot page","title":"Player cards, guilds and totals","summary":"Understand the information shown for each looter.","body":"<p>Each player card shows the character name, captured guild/alliance when available, group labels, item types, total quantity and latest loot time. Loaded files preserve guild fields such as <code>guild</code>, <code>guild_name</code>, <code>guildName</code> and <code>looted_by_guild</code>. Players can be collapsed individually or automatically when first seen.</p>"},{"id":"item-cards","cat":"Loot page","title":"Item cards and item details","summary":"Inspect names, IDs, quantities, value, source and history.","body":"<p>Item cards can show icon, item name, tier/enchantment, quality, category, Albion item ID, quantity, estimated silver, source and edit/note indicators. Clicking an item opens the detail modal with pickup history, source and time. Right-click opens correction actions such as edit, move, source/category change, note, deposit state, duplicate/invalid flag and delete where supported.</p>"},{"id":"loot-filters","cat":"Loot page","title":"Search, category tabs and quick filters","summary":"Change only the view without deleting session data.","body":"<ul><li>The main search matches player, guild, alliance, item, item ID and source.</li><li>Category tabs include all loot, gear & mounts, resources, food & potions and other.</li><li>Recent 5m shows only recently captured events.</li><li>Pinned keeps manually pinned entries easy to find.</li><li>Show all players temporarily bypasses tracked-roster visibility without changing the saved roster.</li><li>Workflow filters add tier, enchantment, quality, date range, status and min/max value.</li></ul>"},{"id":"sorting","cat":"Loot page","title":"Sorting, density and collapsing","summary":"Control ordering and card size independently of data.","body":"<table><thead><tr><th>Control</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Player sort</td><td>Latest loot, highest quantity or name A–Z.</td></tr><tr><td>Item sort</td><td>Default/newest, quantity, name or highest silver value.</td></tr><tr><td>Comfortable</td><td>Largest spacing and easiest reading.</td></tr><tr><td>Compact</td><td>Reduced spacing and card height.</td></tr><tr><td>Very compact</td><td>Maximum information density.</td></tr><tr><td>Collapse new players</td><td>Newly discovered player cards start closed.</td></tr><tr><td>Pause view</td><td>Useful while selecting or editing; capture is not paused.</td></tr></tbody></table>"},{"id":"small-view","cat":"Loot page","title":"Small View","summary":"Reduce Loot and Bank Compare to item name and quantity.","body":"<p>Small View is an optional display mode for Loot and Bank Compare. It hides secondary card details so only the item and quantity remain. It does not remove IDs, sources, history, prices or bank status from the stored data; open details or disable Small View to see them again.</p>"},{"id":"load-loot","cat":"Loot page","title":"Load loot logger files","summary":"Add saved loot-events TXT/CSV files directly to the live session.","body":"<p><b>Load loot files</b> accepts logger loot-event files without going through Bank Compare. The same selected merge mode used by Bank Compare is applied. Loaded players keep guild/alliance fields, items are reclassified with the current catalog, icons are resolved when possible and source history is preserved.</p>"},{"id":"merge-modes","cat":"Loot page","title":"Smart, Combine and Sum merge","summary":"Choose how duplicate-looking rows from multiple files are handled.","body":"<table><thead><tr><th>Control</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Smart merge</td><td>Deduplicates matching event signatures and keeps the strongest complete record. Best default.</td></tr><tr><td>Combine merge</td><td>Combines observer files while preserving distinct time/source events and avoiding duplicate observations.</td></tr><tr><td>Sum merge</td><td>Adds quantities from every selected file. Use only when files represent separate, non-overlapping loot.</td></tr></tbody></table>"},{"id":"groups-assign","cat":"Groups","title":"Assign players to persistent groups","summary":"Reuse the same player grouping in future sessions.","body":"<p>Open a player group action to choose one or more existing groups or type a new group. Assignments are saved by player name in local storage and automatically appear when that player is seen in later events. A player may belong to multiple groups.</p>"},{"id":"groups-manager","cat":"Groups","title":"Groups manager","summary":"Create, rename, assign, remove and delete groups centrally.","body":"<p>The <b>Groups</b> button opens a manager where you select a group, view all assigned players, assign a typed player, create and assign a new group, rename the group, remove individual players or delete the group. Deleting a group removes that label from every player but does not delete loot.</p>"},{"id":"bank-workflow","cat":"Bank Compare","title":"Recommended Bank Compare workflow","summary":"Reconcile expected loot against actual deposits.","body":"<ol><li>Capture or load the correct loot session.</li><li>Import the Albion bank export by drop, file picker or clipboard.</li><li>Optionally load additional loot logger files and choose the source/merge mode.</li><li>Review matched, partial, missing, extra, different, resolved, ignored and lost states.</li><li>Check confidence guidance and imported-file provenance.</li><li>Resolve exceptions, copy/export the missing list and archive the completed session.</li></ol>"},{"id":"bank-import","cat":"Bank Compare","title":"Importing bank exports","summary":"Load one or multiple bank files without double-importing them.","body":"<p>Drop bank files onto the import area, choose files, or use <b>Import from clipboard</b>. Multiple files are combined. Exact duplicate file hashes are ignored. A logger loot-events file is rejected from the bank input and must be loaded under Additional loot logger files. <b>Clear comparison</b> removes imported bank data without deleting the loot session.</p>"},{"id":"bank-additional","cat":"Bank Compare","title":"Additional loot logger files","summary":"Choose whether comparison uses loaded files alone or merges them with the current session.","body":"<table><thead><tr><th>Control</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Loaded loot TXT only</td><td>Builds expected loot only from the selected logger files.</td></tr><tr><td>Current session + loaded TXT</td><td>Merges imported loot into the live/loaded session.</td></tr><tr><td>Smart/Combine/Sum</td><td>Uses the merge behavior described in the Loot section.</td></tr><tr><td>Clear files</td><td>Removes only additional logger files and restores the comparison base.</td></tr></tbody></table>"},{"id":"bank-status","cat":"Bank Compare","title":"Deposit states and colors","summary":"Interpret every item state correctly.","body":"<table><thead><tr><th>Control</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Matched · green</td><td>Expected deposited quantity is present.</td></tr><tr><td>Partial · yellow</td><td>Some expected quantity is present; the shown percentage is deposited share.</td></tr><tr><td>Missing · red</td><td>No expected quantity was found.</td></tr><tr><td>Extra</td><td>Bank contains more than expected.</td></tr><tr><td>Different item</td><td>Bank-only item or unmatched item identity.</td></tr><tr><td>Resolved</td><td>Manually reviewed and accepted.</td></tr><tr><td>Ignored</td><td>Excluded from outstanding totals by a deliberate action.</td></tr><tr><td>Lost · grey</td><td>The player looted it, then the item was looted from them after death; owed quantity is reduced.</td></tr></tbody></table>"},{"id":"bank-confidence","cat":"Bank Compare","title":"Exact, Likely and Ambiguous matching","summary":"Use the score as guidance, not as a probability.","body":"<p><b>Exact 100%</b> means player, item, enchantment and expected quantity directly agree. <b>Likely</b> means one candidate is stronger than alternatives. <b>Ambiguous</b> means multiple players or stacks could plausibly match. A Partial percentage describes deposited share, not confidence. Hover the label for the rule explanation.</p>"},{"id":"bank-roster","cat":"Bank Compare","title":"Tracked players, guilds and alliances","summary":"Limit Bank Compare with strict current roster matching.","body":"<p>Tracked players match by character name. Tracked guilds and alliances match the current guild/alliance captured in loot or bank data. Resolved guild-member data is used only when the current guild is unavailable. With no custom roster, Bank Compare uses players found in the imported bank export. Inputs are debounced and saved so typing is not overwritten by refreshes.</p>"},{"id":"roster-tools","cat":"Bank Compare","title":"Look up and sync players & guilds","summary":"Verify names, browse alliance guilds and refresh roster data.","body":"<p><b>Look up players & guilds</b> opens a guild picker containing tracked guilds and guilds discovered from tracked alliances, then shows the selected guild roster and allows adding players or the guild. <b>Sync players & guilds</b> refreshes tracked player matches, guild rosters and alliance guild lists. Choose the correct Albion server: Europe, Americas or Asia.</p>"},{"id":"bank-dashboard","cat":"Bank Compare","title":"Completion dashboard and suggestions","summary":"See outstanding totals, value and import provenance.","body":"<p>The Workflow bank dashboard shows expected, deposited, partial outstanding, missing, completion percentage and missing value. It ranks the highest outstanding value, lists every imported bank file and offers approve/reject suggestions. Approving creates a visible manual resolution with a note and provenance.</p>"},{"id":"bank-actions","cat":"Bank Compare","title":"Search, sorting, details and manual actions","summary":"Finish reconciliation without losing audit history.","body":"<ul><li>Filter by all, missing, partial, matched, extra, different, resolved or ignored.</li><li>Sort by status, newest, quantity, name or silver value.</li><li>Expand/collapse all players or one player.</li><li>Click an item for the same detailed information used in Loot.</li><li>Copy missing list or export a comparison report.</li><li>Manual status/note changes remain visible and are included in saves and exports.</li></ul>"},{"id":"banklogs-workflow","cat":"Bank Logs Compare","title":"Temporary banks to final bank","summary":"Track responsibility across temporary chests and one final destination.","body":"<p>Load every temporary chest log that records withdrawals and remaining responsibility, then load one final-bank log. The page calculates what each player was responsible for and compares that expected quantity with the final bank. The comparison is intentionally temporary and is cleared when the application closes.</p>"},{"id":"banklogs-status","cat":"Bank Logs Compare","title":"Bank Logs Compare calculations","summary":"Understand expected, final, missing, extra and final-only results.","body":"<table><thead><tr><th>Control</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Matched</td><td>Final amount equals expected responsibility.</td></tr><tr><td>Partial</td><td>Final amount is above zero but below expected.</td></tr><tr><td>Missing</td><td>Nothing expected was found in final.</td></tr><tr><td>Extra</td><td>Final has more than expected.</td></tr><tr><td>Final-only / Different</td><td>An item exists in final without temporary responsibility.</td></tr><tr><td>Temporary responsibility</td><td>Withdrawn quantity adjusted for items still attributed in temporary logs.</td></tr></tbody></table>"},{"id":"banklogs-controls","cat":"Bank Logs Compare","title":"Files, filters and Copy missing","summary":"Operate the temporary comparison page.","body":"<ul><li>Choose, paste or drag multiple temporary logs; exact duplicate files are ignored.</li><li>Choose, paste or drag one final log.</li><li>Remove individual temporary files or clear temporary/final/all.</li><li>Search responsible player, item or temporary filename.</li><li>Filter status, expand/collapse players and copy a Discord-ready missing report.</li><li>Ctrl+F or / focuses search while this page is active.</li></ul>"},{"id":"price-settings","cat":"Prices and value","title":"Estimated value settings","summary":"Select the market context used for item estimates.","body":"<p>Estimated values use the configured Albion server, market city, quality behavior and order side. Supported cities include Thetford, Fort Sterling, Lymhurst, Martlock, Bridgewatch and Caerleon. When Show estimated values is enabled, the logger periodically checks loaded items and refreshes missing/stale values.</p>"},{"id":"price-cache","cat":"Prices and value","title":"Cache, fallback chain and manual prices","summary":"Know where a displayed price came from.","body":"<p>The price panel shows cache entries, city, cache age, missing item count and current total value. Refresh missing only, refresh all or clear the cache. Manual price fallback stores silver per item by item ID and optional quality. The fallback chain can use selected market, historical cache, regional alternatives, opposite order side and Black Market according to enabled settings.</p>"},{"id":"historical-value","cat":"Prices and value","title":"Historical session value","summary":"Compare the saved event estimate with current prices.","body":"<p>Archived sessions keep a value snapshot so later market changes do not rewrite the original event estimate. The historical panel can show saved value, current recalculated value, missing prices and the difference. Manual prices are visibly marked as a fallback source.</p>"},{"id":"session-manager","cat":"Sessions and archives","title":"Session Manager","summary":"Load, save, rename, duplicate and organize sessions.","body":"<p>Session Manager lists stored sessions and their metadata. Selecting a session shows name, guild, event/content, zone, start/end, players, quantity, value, tags and favourite state. Changes are saved as a draft automatically; use the explicit save/archive action when the event should become a durable archive.</p>"},{"id":"session-metadata","cat":"Sessions and archives","title":"Session details, notes and autosave","summary":"Preserve context that packet capture cannot know.","body":"<p>Use session name, guild, event, content, zone, notes, tags and favourite state to make archives searchable. Autosave protects the active session and stores unfinished recovery data. Session notes are local and are included in complete backups.</p>"},{"id":"archives","cat":"Sessions and archives","title":"Archive search and preview","summary":"Find a past event without loading every file manually.","body":"<p>Search archives by name, date, guild, player, item, zone or tag. Filter by minimum saved value or favourites only. Preview displays metadata, players, quantity, value and validation information before loading. Reload archives refreshes the list from storage.</p>"},{"id":"templates","cat":"Sessions and archives","title":"Templates, saved views, tags and favourites","summary":"Reuse recurring event settings and layouts.","body":"<p>Session templates can save metadata and recurring configuration. Saved views preserve grouping, density, minimum silver, card width, column order and column visibility. Tags improve search; favourites pin important sessions. Apply a template/view before an event, then change only what differs.</p>"},{"id":"merge-sessions","cat":"Sessions and archives","title":"Merge sessions","summary":"Combine related captures while preserving provenance.","body":"<p>Merge can combine selected sessions into one archive. Duplicate event signatures are checked so the same captured/imported event is not silently counted twice. Review validation and totals after merging, especially when source files overlap.</p>"},{"id":"split-sessions","cat":"Sessions and archives","title":"Split sessions","summary":"Create focused archives by player, time, zone or name.","body":"<p>Advanced split supports one session per player, before/after a selected time, zone and player-search splits. Timeline selection can set the earliest selected event as the split point. Split archives receive new IDs and preserve event metadata.</p>"},{"id":"backup","cat":"Sessions and archives","title":"Complete backup, restore and trash","summary":"Protect sessions, settings and local application state.","body":"<p>A complete backup includes the active session, archived sessions, backup records, trash and relevant <code>albion-</code>, <code>all70-</code> and <code>all80-</code> settings. Choose a backup folder for automatic/manual backups, use Backup now, and restore only trusted backups. Deleted archives may be retained in trash depending on the action.</p>"},{"id":"imports-exports","cat":"Sessions and archives","title":"Import and export reference","summary":"Choose a format that matches the task.","body":"<table><thead><tr><th>Control</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Export TXT</td><td>Readable loot report with player, guild, source, quantity and time.</td></tr><tr><td>CSV/TSV</td><td>Spreadsheet analysis and custom calculations.</td></tr><tr><td>Copy summary / missing</td><td>Clipboard-ready compact report.</td></tr><tr><td>Selected event/item export</td><td>Only checked records.</td></tr><tr><td>Timeline export</td><td>Chronological audit record.</td></tr><tr><td>Bank report</td><td>Deposit completion and unresolved items.</td></tr><tr><td>Complete backup</td><td>Restorable application data and settings.</td></tr><tr><td>Simulation file</td><td>JSON or loot-events TXT used without live Albion traffic.</td></tr></tbody></table>"},{"id":"workflow-recovery","cat":"Workflow","title":"Capture recovery and duplicate protection","summary":"Restore unfinished work and control duplicate detection.","body":"<p>Workflow shows capture state, last loot and unfinished-session recovery. Restore reopens recoverable data; Dismiss discards the recovery prompt. Duplicate protection uses event signatures and a configurable duplicate window in milliseconds. Skipped and flagged duplicate counts appear in diagnostics.</p>"},{"id":"validation","cat":"Workflow","title":"Session validation","summary":"Find structural errors before Bank Compare or export.","body":"<p>Validation checks missing player/item names, invalid quantities, duplicate-looking events, timestamps outside the session range, inconsistent totals, unknown categories, unresolved bank states and other data-quality issues. Findings are grouped as error, warning and info. Copy error report creates a technical report for troubleshooting.</p>"},{"id":"corrections","cat":"Workflow","title":"Manual correction and context actions","summary":"Add missed loot or repair a wrong record without hiding the change.","body":"<p>Manual correction can add player, guild, item name/ID, quantity, source, category and time. Right-click item actions can edit, move player, correct source/category, add note, mark deposited, flag invalid/duplicate or delete. Edited records receive visible markers and remain part of undo, timeline, validation, archives and exports.</p>"},{"id":"multi-select","cat":"Workflow","title":"Multi-select actions","summary":"Apply one audited change to several items.","body":"<p>Selection actions include Move player, Correct source, Change category, Mark deposited, Add note, Export selected and Delete. The selected count is shown. Bank Compare deliberately avoids Loot selection checkboxes where they would conflict with deposit controls.</p>"},{"id":"undo-redo","cat":"Workflow","title":"Undo and redo","summary":"Recover from accidental full actions.","body":"<p>The full-action history stores before/after snapshots for supported edits, imports, bank assignments and selected-event removal. <b>Ctrl+Z</b> undoes the latest action and <b>Ctrl+Y</b> reapplies it. History is intentionally limited, so verify destructive actions promptly.</p>"},{"id":"timeline","cat":"Workflow","title":"Timeline and ownership chain","summary":"Trace when an item moved and who became responsible.","body":"<p>Timeline lists chronological pickup events with player, guild, item, quantity, source and time. Search, export, select events, remove selected quantities or set a split point. Ownership chains distinguish pickups, deposits and death transfers; lost-after-death events reduce owed quantity and use grey styling.</p>"},{"id":"view-controls","cat":"Workflow","title":"Grouping, columns and saved views","summary":"Customize Loot and Bank Compare separately.","body":"<p>Grouping can show grouped items, every event, source groups, quality groups or a time window. Density, minimum silver, card width and column order are configurable. Columns include icon, name, quantity, category, ID, source, value, status, confidence and note, with separate Loot/Bank visibility.</p>"},{"id":"tests-logs","cat":"Workflow","title":"Self-test, diagnostic logs and error overlay","summary":"Collect useful evidence when a button or background action fails.","body":"<p>Self-test checks core storage, rendering, price/cache paths and application services. The diagnostic log records actions, warnings and errors and can be filtered, copied, exported or cleared. Unhandled errors show a visible overlay with the failed action, message, Copy report and Dismiss controls.</p>"},{"id":"advanced-health","cat":"Advanced","title":"Advanced Control Center health","summary":"Use the stable health cards and downloadable diagnostics.","body":"<p>Advanced repeats the most important health indicators in stable cards so only values update and the layout does not flicker. Capture diagnostic snapshot records the current state; Download diagnostics writes a technical report containing platform, session, capture, catalog, prices, validation and recent errors.</p>"},{"id":"simulation","cat":"Advanced","title":"Test simulation","summary":"Replay loot without Albion or packet capture.","body":"<p>Load a test JSON or loot-events TXT, choose replay speed, start from the beginning, pause/resume or stop. Simulation feeds the normal Loot, Analytics, Bank Compare and correction paths, making it suitable for testing icons, categories, guild names, value estimates and UI behavior. Live capture mode is restored when simulation stops.</p>"},{"id":"skipped","cat":"Advanced","title":"Skipped loot inspector","summary":"Review rejected events without constant refresh interrupting selection.","body":"<p>The inspector lists skipped events by reason, including unknown source, duplicate event, invalid quantity and parser rules. Filter reasons, inspect Raw data, clear the list or Allow item when a valid item was incorrectly rejected. Rendering waits while you are interacting so dropdown/selection input is not swallowed.</p>"},{"id":"unknown-items","cat":"Advanced","title":"Unknown item recovery","summary":"Rename and classify catalog misses.","body":"<p>Unknown item recovery shows unresolved item IDs, current display name and category. Enable Keep unclassified items visible for review, enter a better name, select a category and Save. Update item database refreshes the known catalog. Long IDs wrap instead of widening the panel.</p>"},{"id":"safe-mode","cat":"Advanced","title":"Safe Mode and reset categories","summary":"Recover from damaged startup state with the smallest reset possible.","body":"<p>Safe Mode disables automatic loaded-session restoration, icon downloads, price refresh, packet event intake and custom layout effects. Repeated unclean starts can trigger it automatically. Reset categories include interface, capture helpers, tracked roster, market cache, templates or everything. Disable Safe Mode and restart to restore all services.</p>"},{"id":"advanced-settings","cat":"Advanced","title":"Ignored items, inactivity and backup retention","summary":"Persist advanced text/number settings without losing typed input.","body":"<p>Advanced settings such as ignored categories/items, inactivity minutes and backup count commit after typing stops rather than rerendering over the field. Ignored rules should be narrow and deliberate because they can prevent events from reaching Loot.</p>"},{"id":"analytics","cat":"Analytics","title":"Analytics page","summary":"Read event performance and market summaries.","body":"<p>Analytics shows runtime, visible players, item types, quantity, session/capture details, top looters, top items, the six most expensive items, recent activity and local session notes. Results follow active category/source/roster filters, while stored session totals remain unchanged. Reload refreshes the page; Restart capture restarts the packet listener.</p>"},{"id":"analytics-diagnostics","cat":"Analytics","title":"Diagnostics and loot trace","summary":"Use Analytics for quick operational checks.","body":"<p>Diagnostics + loot trace summarizes the pipeline from capture through decoded events and host/other-player counts. Use it to determine whether a missing item failed at packet intake, Albion recognition, event decoding, source validation, category filtering or rendering.</p>"},{"id":"themes","cat":"Options and appearance","title":"Interface themes","summary":"Choose from 50 colour and Albion side-art themes.","body":"<p>The Interface theme dropdown contains 50 presets, including dark/light palettes and Albion-themed side art. Theme selection is saved automatically and applied across Loot, Bank Compare, Bank Logs Compare, Options, Analytics, Advanced, Workflow and Help. Light mode receives dedicated readable field, card and help styling.</p>"},{"id":"backgrounds","cat":"Options and appearance","title":"Background image folder","summary":"Use a local wallpaper without removing the selected theme.","body":"<p>Choose a folder containing 1920×1080 images. Supported extensions include PNG, APNG, JPG/JPEG/JFIF, WebP, AVIF, GIF, BMP, SVG and ICO. Files are sorted by name; Next image cycles them. The folder is checked about every ten seconds, the selected filename is remembered, and Clear removes folder access and the wallpaper. A saved folder may require permission again after restart.</p>"},{"id":"interface-options","cat":"Options and appearance","title":"Interface and display options","summary":"Configure visible information and optional pages.","body":"<ul><li>Show live capture pipeline, loot popups and skipped-packet messages.</li><li>Show Albion item IDs.</li><li>Compact item cards, Small View and collapse new players.</li><li>Enable or hide Analytics, Advanced, Workflow and Help pages.</li><li>Choose player/item sorting and minimum total quantity shown.</li><li>Options save automatically after a short delay; Save options forces an immediate commit and Reset defaults restores defaults.</li></ul>"},{"id":"capture-options","cat":"Options and appearance","title":"Loot sources, categories and automatic sessions","summary":"Control what enters or appears in the session.","body":"<p>Host character and Other players can be enabled independently. Item categories include equipment, mounts, resources, potions, food, trash, journals/books, artifacts/tokens and other/unknown. Automatic session settings include startup new session, inactivity handling and optional Albion start/close lifecycle. Turning off a category hides or rejects it according to the relevant option; use validation and skipped inspector when testing changes.</p>"},{"id":"persistence","cat":"Options and appearance","title":"What persists after restart","summary":"Know which settings are local and which comparisons are temporary.","body":"<p>Themes, wallpaper selection, transparency, groups, tracked roster, page visibility, sorting, saved filters/views, templates, manual prices, notes, archives and many advanced settings persist locally. Bank Logs Compare temporary/final files do not persist. Complete backup is the supported way to move or restore local data. No gameplay credentials are required by these interface features.</p>"},{"id":"trouble-capture","cat":"Troubleshooting","title":"No packets or Albion not detected","summary":"Follow the capture chain in order.","body":"<ol><li>Confirm Npcap is installed and compatible.</li><li>Run the logger with sufficient permissions.</li><li>Start Albion and enter the world.</li><li>Restart capture and inspect available interfaces.</li><li>Raw packets at zero means interface/Npcap; raw rising but Albion UDP zero means wrong traffic/interface; UDP rising but no events means decoder/source rules.</li><li>Copy a diagnostic report before restarting if the issue persists.</li></ol>"},{"id":"trouble-loot","cat":"Troubleshooting","title":"Loot is missing, duplicated or assigned incorrectly","summary":"Check filters and evidence before editing totals.","body":"<ol><li>Clear search, category, recent, roster and minimum-value filters.</li><li>Open Skipped loot inspector for unknown source, duplicate or invalid quantity.</li><li>Inspect item details and ownership timeline.</li><li>Verify loaded files and merge mode; Sum can double overlapping files.</li><li>Use validation and duplicate report.</li><li>Correct with audited edit/flag actions rather than silently changing exports.</li></ol>"},{"id":"trouble-bank","cat":"Troubleshooting","title":"Bank comparison looks wrong","summary":"Reset only the comparison and re-import chronologically.","body":"<ol><li>Confirm the correct loot session or additional loot files are selected.</li><li>Check source mode and merge mode.</li><li>Review imported bank provenance and duplicate-file warnings.</li><li>Confirm tracked roster/current guild/alliance matching.</li><li>Understand Partial percentage vs confidence.</li><li>Clear comparison, import bank files in chronological order and validate again.</li></ol>"},{"id":"trouble-assets","cat":"Troubleshooting","title":"Icons, prices, themes or wallpaper are missing","summary":"Separate catalog, market and appearance causes.","body":"<ul><li>Icons: check Catalog/Lookup, refresh items and disable Safe Mode.</li><li>Prices: verify server/city/quality/order side, refresh missing, inspect fallback and manual price.</li><li>Theme: reselect the theme and verify interface reset was not used.</li><li>Wallpaper: reconnect folder permission, verify supported extension and use Next image.</li><li>Transparency: Off/See Through/True See Through are mutually exclusive; the wallpaper should remain visible in both transparent modes.</li></ul>"},{"id":"trouble-startup","cat":"Troubleshooting","title":"Black screen, broken layout or repeated startup failure","summary":"Recover without deleting all data first.","body":"<ol><li>Wait briefly for the embedded UI decoder; if the window stays blank, close it cleanly and restart.</li><li>Use Safe Mode after repeated unclean starts.</li><li>Reset Interface only before resetting Everything.</li><li>Export a complete backup whenever the UI becomes usable.</li><li>Download diagnostics and include the application version shown in Help/Workflow/Advanced.</li></ol>"},{"id":"data-reference","cat":"Reference","title":"Important fields and audit markers","summary":"Understand terms used throughout the logger.","body":"<table><thead><tr><th>Control</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Expected / owed</td><td>Quantity attributed to a player after death-transfer adjustments.</td></tr><tr><td>Deposited / bank amount</td><td>Quantity found in imported bank data.</td></tr><tr><td>Source</td><td>Character or origin the item was looted from.</td></tr><tr><td>Pickup history</td><td>Individual event times, sources and quantities behind a grouped card.</td></tr><tr><td>Manual edit</td><td>User-created or changed record; visibly marked.</td></tr><tr><td>Duplicate / invalid</td><td>Flagged record excluded from normal totals but retained in audit data.</td></tr><tr><td>Provenance</td><td>File names/actions that produced a comparison or resolution.</td></tr><tr><td>Value snapshot</td><td>Price estimate saved with an archive at that time.</td></tr></tbody></table>"}],features=["Live packet capture through Npcap","Npcap missing/outdated compatibility prompt","Albion process detection","Raw packet and Albion UDP counters","Photon/event/response diagnostics","Exact last-loot age","Host-character detection","Host and other-player source toggles","Unknown-source rejection","Duplicate-event protection","Configurable duplicate window","Live loot popups","Skipped-packet notifications","Pause visual updates","Manual capture restart","New/clear/automatic sessions","Startup new-session option","Albion close/start lifecycle option","Inactivity auto-end","Session runtime and status bar","Player/guild/alliance display","Guild restoration from loaded files","Persistent multi-group assignments","Groups manager create/rename/delete","Player card collapse/expand","Collapse new players by default","Small View","Comfortable/compact/very compact density","Search across players/guilds/items/sources","Category tabs and recent/pinned filters","Tier/enchantment/quality/date/value filters","Saved filter presets","Player and item sorting","Silver-value sorting","Custom card width","Separate Loot/Bank columns","Saved view presets","Item detail modal","Pickup history and source time","Right-click correction menu","Manual loot creation","Multi-select bulk actions","Visible edit/note markers","Full-action undo/redo","Timeline search/export","Timeline event selection","Ownership/death/deposit chains","Lost-after-death owed reduction","Load loot logger files on Loot","Smart merge","Combine observer merge","Sum merge","Bank export drag/drop","Multiple bank-file combination","Clipboard bank import","Duplicate bank-file rejection","Additional loot logger files in Bank Compare","Current-session or file-only expected source","Matched/partial/missing/extra/different/resolved/ignored states","Green/yellow/red/grey status borders","Exact/Likely/Ambiguous guidance","Strict tracked player/guild/alliance roster","Guild/alliance lookup picker","Player/guild/alliance sync","Bank completion KPIs","Missing-value ranking","Import provenance","Approve/reject assignment suggestions","Copy/export missing bank list","Temporary-vs-final Bank Logs Compare","Temporary bank duplicate prevention","Bank Logs status/search/copy missing","Market server/city settings","Estimated value periodic refresh","Price cache age and missing count","Refresh missing/all prices","Manual per-item price fallback","Fallback chain settings","Historical archived value snapshot","Analytics top looters/items","Top six expensive items","Recent activity and notes","Stable Advanced capture-health cards","Capture diagnostic snapshot","Download diagnostics","Test simulation JSON/TXT","Replay speed/pause/stop","Skipped loot inspector","Raw skipped-event view","Allow rejected item","Unknown item rename/category recovery","Update item database","Keep unclassified items visible","Session Manager drafts and metadata","Archive search/preview","Tags and favourites","Session templates","Merge sessions","Split by player/time/zone/name","Complete local backup","Backup folder and retention","Restore and trash data","Self-test wizard","Searchable diagnostic logs","Visible unhandled-error overlay","Safe Mode","Category-specific resets","50 interface themes","Albion side-art themes","Local background-image folder","Automatic folder rescanning","Next/Clear background image","See Through blur mode","True See Through no-blur mode","Transparency on every page","Optional page visibility","Automatic option saving","Searchable Help manual","Help expand/collapse and topic navigation","TXT/CSV/timeline/selected exports"];
